# Everything under scripts/pbx runs on the Linux PBX, and the installer carries
# an embedded byte-for-byte copy of vitalpbx-inbound-route-helper.py guarded by
# a byte-identity test (install-vitalpbx-inbound-route-helper.test.ts).
#
# On Windows, core.autocrlf=true checks the .sh out as CRLF while the .py stays
# LF, so that guard can never pass locally — it fails by construction, gets
# ignored, and the embedded helper silently drifts. It drifted twice: to
# 2026.07.26.1 (missing apply_tenant_changes entirely) and again to 2026.08.06.2
# while the live PBX ran 2026.08.06.6, where running the installer would have
# DOWNGRADED the PBX and wiped the doorway-hijack fix.
#
# Deliberately scoped to scripts/pbx rather than a repo-wide *.sh rule: 113 shell
# scripts elsewhere are CRLF in working trees and a blanket flip would churn
# unrelated in-flight work.
/scripts/pbx/** text eol=lf

# docs/pbx carries reference copies of scripts and Asterisk .conf that get
# scp'd to the Linux PBX (media-sync, prompt-sync, voicemail-drop context).
# Same CRLF trap as above, same scoped fix — .sh and .conf only, so the .md
# files keep normal Windows behavior. Added 2026-08-12 when docs/ stopped
# being gitignored wholesale.
/docs/pbx/*.sh text eol=lf
/docs/pbx/*.conf text eol=lf

# Regenerated from Linux PBX dumps and diffed against fresh ones — keep LF so a
# re-dump compares byte-for-byte.
/scripts/deskPhoneSetup/** text eol=lf

# CLAUDE.md contains a NUL byte (a `\0` written through a shell heredoc in 2026-08),
# so git's binary auto-detection exempts it from core.autocrlf conversion and it
# stores whatever line endings the last tool happened to write. That made it flip
# CRLF (d39cad7f..38c618b1) -> LF (69ae1b37) on a FORTY-LINE content change, rendering
# as 20,618 insertions / 20,577 deletions.
#
# ⛔ That is a safety problem, not a tidiness one: this repo's rule is to read the
# staged diff before every commit, because it is the only thing that catches another
# session's in-flight CLAUDE.md work being swept in — and a whole-file line-ending
# diff cannot be read. It would keep flip-flopping every time a different tool wrote
# the file.
#
# An explicit `text` overrides the binary auto-detection, so git now normalises to LF
# in the blob whatever is on disk and the churn stops. The blob is ALREADY LF as of
# 69ae1b37, so this costs zero churn to add. It also makes the NUL repair (see the
# CLAUDE.md section about itself) a content-only change whenever somebody does it.
/CLAUDE.md text eol=lf

# Loopcom Community apps: LF everywhere (Linux server, Docker builds)
apps/community-api/** text eol=lf
apps/community-web/** text eol=lf
infra/community/** text eol=lf
docs/community/** text eol=lf
